  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Five editorial storefronts",
    "overview": "Five fictional businesses share clear controls and a visible Crealia connection while keeping their own palette, photographic composition and voice. This scoped system records the implemented world in `demo.css` and `demo.js`; it does not replace the root Crealia design system.\n\nThe approved direction uses large type, uneven photographic pairs and generous space around practical interactions. Distrito is precise and dark, Forma is a fashion lookbook, Brasa is bold and appetizing, Miga is relaxed, and Aura is calm. These are illustrative concepts, never client evidence.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Distinct brand palettes over a common semantic theme.",
      "Editorial photography with unequal image sizes.",
      "One useful simulation per business.",
      "Visible content before animation or JavaScript."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Theme Rule",
